        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Runs each selected child in turn and merges what they produce :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

The merge is the same one :cpp:func:`IniFile::fix` performs over its own per-mod-type
fixers: a later child writing the same file path simply overwrites an earlier one

.. note::
   Children are invoked through the public :cpp:func:`BaseIniFixer::fix`, which fixes
   *with* boilerplate and *with* the source content. &apos;withBoilerPlate&apos; and &apos;withSrc&apos;
   are therefore **not** propagated to them -- ``fixImpl`` is protected, so a child&apos;s
   cannot be reached from here. This matches how :cpp:func:`IniFile::fix` invokes its
   own fixers, which is the behaviour this method mirrors
</verbatim></para>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Does the actual fixing -- the customization point behind #fix, and the direct
equivalent of the pure-Python original&apos;s ``_fix``. Returns an empty map by default,
matching that original&apos;s ``pass``
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>parseData</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parse data to fix from <ndash/> see <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_multi_mod_fixer_1a3e016e4127345f92b275fec909e7ae00" kindref="member">ParseData</ref> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>keepBackup</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to keep backups for the .ini file </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fixOnly</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to only fix the .ini file without undoing any fixes </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>hideOrig</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to hide the mod for the original character </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>withBoilerPlate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to include the surrounding boilerplate in the result </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>withSrc</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to include the .ini file&apos;s original content in the result </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fixingCtx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The per-call options for this fix <ndash/> see :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_ini_fixing_context" kindref="compound">IniFixingContext</ref></computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The new content of the fixed .ini file(s), keyed by file path    </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
